From c05a16c50ede9504b88b97fd42b60318ac882ce5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 05:47:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scanner: fix PNG/JPEG photo mime bug, move result photo +
 logo to full-viewport layers

- Root-cause fix: employees.photo_thumb_b64 was always labeled
  image/jpeg in data: URIs, but Drive's /thumbnail endpoint returns
  PNG for a real fraction of employees. Added sniffImageMimeFromBase64()/
  photoDataUri() in Utils/image.js to read the real magic bytes instead
  of assuming; wired into offlineAvatarHTML() (format.js) and the
  Scanner's hero-photo swap.
- Moved the matched-scan result photo out of the small .ss-icon ring
  into a new fixed, full-viewport .ss-photo-stage sized off
  min(82dvh,82dvw), centered, independent of the 3-column kiosk layout.
- Moved the Proximity logo mark out of .ss-icon into a new fixed,
  full-viewport .ss-bg-logo background layer; .ss-icon is now just the
  empty center point for the idle pulsing ring.
- Updated README.md and Supabase/README.md change logs/schema notes.
